# Hand-authored, validation-ONLY structural facts about schema.org terms.
#
# schema.org is CC-BY-SA-3.0 → REFERENCE_ONLY under the project's license policy
# (config.policy_for_license), so its axioms must never be vendored under
# imports/targets/ (refresh_snapshot refuses it) and must never enter the
# published CC BY 4.0 artifact. This file lives under tests/fixtures/ and is read
# only by the native SSSOM alignment-direction linter.
#
# It asserts only the handful of *structural facts* (inverse pairs + soft
# domain/range) needed to catch direction errors offline — no labels, no
# descriptions, no prose. These are facts, not a republication of schema.org.
# The full vocabulary is fetched live under the `network` test mark / --network.

@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# The org-hierarchy inverse pair behind the motivating bug (#25): GMEOW maps
# gmeow:subOrganizationOf (child→parent) to BOTH schema:parentOrganization (the
# correct, equivalent direction) and schema:subOrganization (the inverse). These
# two schema.org terms are mutually inverse — so mapping one property to both is
# the self-contradiction the linter flags.
schema:subOrganization
    rdf:type schema:Property ;
    schema:inverseOf schema:parentOrganization ;
    schema:domainIncludes schema:Organization ;
    schema:rangeIncludes schema:Organization .

schema:parentOrganization
    rdf:type schema:Property ;
    schema:inverseOf schema:subOrganization ;
    schema:domainIncludes schema:Organization ;
    schema:rangeIncludes schema:Organization .
